<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dragiša Cvetković</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dragiša Cvetković was a Serbian politician who served as prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> from 1939 to 1941. He concluded the 1939 agreement with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladko-macek">Vladko Maček</a> that created the Banovina of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, and under heavy German pressure his government signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact">Tripartite Pact</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> on 25 March 1941. He was overthrown two days later by the coup of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dusan-simovic">Dušan Simović</a> and died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dragisa-cvetkovic.jpg" alt="Dragiša Cvetković" width="212" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dragi%C5%A1a_Cvetkovi%C4%87_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
